-- | Subscriptions for a terminal UI program.
--
-- Everything `Sub` offers (`none`, `batch`, `every`, `map`, `subscribeTopic`,
-- `subscribeWebSocket`), plus `onKey` for keyboard input. Combine sources
-- with `Sub.batch`, e.g. `Sub.batch [ Sub.every 1000 Tick, Sub.onKey Key ]`.
module TeaTuiSub exposing
    ( onKey
    )


import Ipe.Ffi.Kernel as Kernel


-- | Deliver each key the user presses as a `{ kind, value }` record.
--
-- `kind` names the key and `value` carries its detail; `value` is `""` unless
-- noted:
--
--   * `"char"` — a printable character; `value` is that character (`"q"`,
--     `"é"`).
--   * `"space"` — the space bar (`value` is `""`, not `" "`).
--   * `"enter"`, `"tab"`, `"backspace"`, `"escape"`, `"delete"`.
--   * `"up"`, `"down"`, `"left"`, `"right"`, `"home"`, `"end"`, `"pageup"`,
--     `"pagedown"`.
--   * `"fn"` — a function key; `value` is its number, `"1"` to `"12"`.
--   * `"ctrl"` — Ctrl with a letter; `value` is the lowercase letter (`"c"`
--     for Ctrl-C). Ctrl-H arrives as `"backspace"`, Ctrl-I as `"tab"`, and
--     Ctrl-J and Ctrl-M as `"enter"`.
--   * `"paste-start"`, `"paste-end"` — the edges of a bracketed paste.
--   * `"other"` — any sequence not listed above; `value` is its raw text.
--
-- Modifiers are not reported on their own: Shift shows only in the character
-- it produces, Alt with a character arrives as `"escape"` and then that
-- character, and a modifier held with a named key (Ctrl-Right) is dropped.
-- Mouse events never reach `onKey`.
--
-- While the view shows focusable controls, the runtime keeps the keys that
-- drive them: Tab and Shift-Tab (and Up and Down outside a text field) move
-- focus, Enter and Space activate the focused control, and while a text field
-- has focus every key goes to the field. A `"ctrl"` key always reaches
-- `onKey`.
onKey =
    Kernel.kernel "TeaTuiSub_onKey"
